HermitCrabInput.dtd
  Based on Maxwell, Mike. 1999. Hermit Crab Parsing Engine Specification.
  SIL manuscript. The DTD describes the input format of the HermitCrab parsing
  engine (https://github.com/sillsdev/machine).

FieldWorks witnesses (edge-cases/*/fieldworks/, languages/*/fieldworks/)
  Each project.fwdata is a small FieldWorks Language Explorer project, written
  by FieldWorks (https://github.com/sillsdev/FieldWorks, LGPL-2.1) on top of
  LibLCM (https://github.com/sillsdev/liblcm, LGPL-2.1). The files hold only
  invented test data plus the standard lists and defaults that FieldWorks and
  LibLCM write into every new project. The versions are in PROVENANCE.md.

Writing system files (fieldworks/WritingSystemStore/*.ldml)
  LDML files written by LibLCM from the SIL Locale Data Repository, which
  carries data from the Unicode Common Locale Data Repository (CLDR). Their
  collation and character data derive from Unicode CLDR data files, copyright
  (c) Unicode, Inc., distributed under the Unicode License v3
  (https://www.unicode.org/license.txt). They are reduced to the elements that
  define the writing system (see AGENTS.md section 3).

Citations
  Grammar and word files cite published linguistic descriptions, and the
  FieldWorks loader source (HCLoader.cs), by name and line only; none of their
  text is copied.
